const entrySeeds = [
  { id:1,g:"g001",type:"primary",word:"resemble",ipa:"/rɪˈzembəl/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to be similar to someone or something in appearance, character, or pattern",coreZh:"在外形、性质或模式上像……",grammar:"及物动词，直接接宾语：A resembles B；不可说 resemble to。",image:"两张不同照片的轮廓逐渐重合。",c:[["closely resemble","酷似","The new district closely resembles the old town in layout.","新区的布局酷似老城。"],["resemble a pattern","呈现类似模式","The decline resembles the pattern observed in rural areas.","这一下降与农村地区观察到的模式相似。"]],origin:"经古法语 resembler，最终与拉丁语 similis（相似）相关；re- 不是现代可自由替换前缀。",family:["resemblance","resembling"],bridge:"熟词桥：resemblance 是“相似之处”，动词 resemble 就是“呈现这种相似”。",scene:"两座城市戴着同一张街道网面具。",landing:"强调相像，不表示同一。",brake:"resemble 后不接 to；需要 be 时改用 be similar to。",micro:["The two systems resemble each other but are not identical.","两个系统彼此相似，但并不相同。"],ie:[["The housing trend resembles that recorded in other rapidly growing cities.","这一住房趋势与其他快速发展城市的记录相似。","Reading","paraphrase"],["The device resembles a watch, although its main function is medical monitoring.","该设备外形像手表，但主要功能是医疗监测。","Speaking","Part 2 description"]]},
  { id:2,g:"g001",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"similar to",linked:"resemble",ipa:"/ˈsɪmələ tə/",pos:"adj. phrase",coreEn:"sharing important features with something else without being identical",coreZh:"与……相似，但并非完全相同",grammar:"similar 是形容词，通常由 be/seem/remain 等系动词承载，比较对象前用 to；可说 similar in size。",image:"两个圆大面积重叠，却各留一块不同区域。",c:[["be broadly similar to","与……大体相似","The two surveys are broadly similar to each other in design.","两项调查在设计上大体相似。"],["be similar in size","尺寸相近","The two samples were similar in size but not in composition.","两个样本大小相近，但构成不同。"]],origin:"similar 来自拉丁语 similis（相似的）；to 标记比较对象。",family:["similar","similarity","similarly","dissimilar"],bridge:"熟词桥：similarity 是“相似性”，similar to 就是“与……有相似性”。",scene:"两条折线几乎重合，却在终点分开。",landing:"比较共同特征，同时保留差异。",brake:"标准搭配是 similar to，不是 similar with；也不要写 resemble to。",micro:["The results are similar to ours, not identical to them.","这些结果与我们的相似，但并不完全相同。"],ie:[["Urban households showed a response similar to that of rural households.","城市家庭的反应与农村家庭相似。","Writing","Task 1 comparison"],["My hometown is similar to the capital in climate, but it is much quieter.","我的家乡气候与首都相似，但安静得多。","Speaking","Part 1 comparison"]]},
  { id:3,g:"g002",type:"primary",word:"recognize",ipa:"/ˈrekəɡnaɪz/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to identify something known before, or formally accept that something is true or valid",coreZh:"认出；识别；承认或正式认可",grammar:"可接名词、recognize that 从句、recognize A as B；英式也拼 recognise。",image:"大脑把眼前面孔与记忆档案配对，并盖上“已确认”印章。",c:[["recognize a face","认出面孔","Most infants recognize a familiar face within seconds.","多数婴儿数秒内就能认出熟悉的面孔。"],["recognize the need for","认识到……的必要性","Governments increasingly recognize the need for cleaner transport.","各国政府日益认识到发展更清洁交通的必要性。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 recognoscere：re-（再次）+ cognoscere（知道、认识）；现代词形中的 cogn 与 cognition 同源。",family:["recognition","recognizable","unrecognized"],bridge:"熟词桥：cognition 是认知；re-cognize 是再次对上已有认知。",scene:"海关扫描一张脸后亮起绿色识别框。",landing:"已有知识与当前对象匹配，或明确接受某事实。",brake:"identify 可首次确定身份；recognize 通常含“以前见过/知道”或“承认有效”。",micro:["Recognize the person, then recognize the problem.","先认出这个人，再承认这个问题。"],ie:[["Researchers now recognize that sleep quality affects academic performance.","研究人员现在承认睡眠质量会影响学业表现。","Reading","claim"],["I recognized the building from a photograph in the travel guide.","我根据旅行指南中的照片认出了那座建筑。","Listening","map context"]]},
  { id:4,g:"g002",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"perceive",linked:"recognize",ipa:"/pəˈsiːv/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to notice through the senses or to interpret something in a particular way",coreZh:"感知；察觉；把……理解为",grammar:"常用 perceive A as B、perceive that；较正式，通常不用进行时表达观念。",image:"眼睛接收同一图像，大脑却贴上不同解释标签。",c:[["perceive a change","察觉变化","Participants perceived a slight change in temperature.","参与者察觉到温度略有变化。"],["be perceived as","被视为","Public transport is often perceived as inconvenient in remote areas.","在偏远地区，公共交通常被视为不方便。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 percipere：per-（完全）+ capere（拿、取得），经法语进入英语。",family:["perception","perceptive","imperceptible"],bridge:"熟词桥：perception 是“感知/看法”；perceive 是形成这种感知。",scene:"同一杯水被两个人分别贴上“半满”和“半空”。",landing:"从感官或解释框架中形成认识。",brake:"perceive 不等于 recognize：前者可首次察觉并解释，后者常与既有记忆匹配。",micro:["We perceive the signal and then interpret it.","我们先感知信号，再解释它。"],ie:[["Residents perceived noise as the main disadvantage of airport expansion.","居民认为噪声是机场扩建的主要弊端。","Writing","Task 2 evidence"],["Some colour differences cannot be perceived under weak artificial light.","在微弱的人造光下，有些颜色差异无法被察觉。","Reading","scientific detail"]]},
  { id:5,g:"g002",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"acknowledge",linked:"recognize",ipa:"/əkˈnɒlɪdʒ/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to accept or state that something is true, or to show that a person or message has been noticed",coreZh:"承认事实；确认收到；认可贡献或在场",grammar:"接名词或 that 从句；acknowledge receipt of 为正式搭配；acknowledge A as B。",image:"收件人盖章“已收到”，又在报告中点名致谢。",c:[["acknowledge a problem","承认问题","The report acknowledges a serious gap in rural healthcare.","报告承认农村医疗存在严重缺口。"],["acknowledge receipt","确认收到","Applicants should acknowledge receipt of the interview invitation.","申请人应确认收到面试邀请。"]],origin:"来自中古英语 aknowen（承认、认知），与 knowledge 有历史联系；ac- 不是现代可自由替换前缀。",family:["acknowledgement","acknowledged","unacknowledged"],bridge:"熟词桥：knowledge 是“知道”；acknowledge 是把知道或接受的事明确表示出来。",scene:"邮箱亮起回执，作者名单旁又盖上感谢印章。",landing:"把事实、消息或贡献明确纳入记录。",brake:"acknowledge receipt 只是确认收到，不自动表示感谢；admit 往往更不情愿。",micro:["Acknowledge the fact, the message, and the people who helped.","承认事实，确认消息，也认可帮助过你的人。"],ie:[["The council acknowledged that the original estimate was unrealistic.","委员会承认最初的估算并不现实。","Writing","Task 2 concession"],["Please acknowledge receipt of the revised timetable before Friday.","请在周五前确认收到修订后的时间表。","Listening","instruction"]]},
  { id:6,g:"g002",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"realize",linked:"recognize",ipa:"/ˈrɪəlaɪz/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to become aware of a fact or to make a plan or ambition real",coreZh:"意识到；实现（计划、目标或价值）",grammar:"认知义常接 that/wh- 从句；实现义接 ambition, potential, value；英式也拼 realise。",image:"头顶灯泡突然亮起，纸上蓝图随后变成实体建筑。",c:[["realize that","意识到","Many commuters realize that cycling is faster at peak times.","许多通勤者意识到高峰期骑车更快。"],["realize the potential","发挥潜力","Better training could help workers realize their full potential.","更好的培训可帮助员工充分发挥潜力。"]],origin:"由 real + -ize 构成；经法语 réaliser 发展出“使成为现实”和“意识到”。",family:["realization","realistic","reality"],bridge:"熟词桥：real 是“真实”；realize 可以是脑中变得真实，也可以把计划变成现实。",scene:"一个想法先在脑中亮灯，再从图纸里站起来。",landing:"从不知道到突然明白，或从设想到现实。",brake:"realize a person 不表示认出某人；认出用 recognize。",micro:["Realize the risk before you realize the plan.","先意识到风险，再实现计划。"],ie:[["Students often realize that regular feedback improves their writing.","学生常意识到定期反馈能改善写作。","Speaking","Part 3 explanation"],["The scheme failed to realize its aim of reducing traffic congestion.","该计划未能实现缓解交通拥堵的目标。","Writing","Task 2 evaluation"]]},
  { id:7,g:"g002",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"appreciate",linked:"recognize",ipa:"/əˈpriːʃieɪt/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to understand the value or seriousness of something, feel grateful for it, or increase in value",coreZh:"理解并重视；感激；升值",grammar:"接名词、appreciate doing、appreciate that；不用 appreciate someone to do；升值义不及物。",image:"一件普通物品被聚光灯照亮，价格牌也缓慢上升。",c:[["appreciate the importance of","理解……的重要性","Young people may not appreciate the importance of preventive care.","年轻人可能尚未充分认识预防保健的重要性。"],["greatly appreciate","非常感激","I would greatly appreciate further information about the course.","如能提供更多课程信息，我将非常感激。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 appretiare：ad-（向）+ pretium（价值、价格），核心历史意象是“定价、重视”。",family:["appreciation","appreciative","depreciate"],bridge:"熟词桥：price 与 pretium 同族意象；appreciate 是看见价值。",scene:"一块不起眼的石头被专家照亮，价格标签翻了十倍。",landing:"价值被理解、感谢或上升。",brake:"appreciate 不等于 acknowledge：前者侧重内心重视/感谢，后者侧重明确表示。",micro:["We appreciate help because we appreciate its value.","我们因理解帮助的价值而心怀感激。"],ie:[["Visitors appreciate the museum more when local history is clearly explained.","当地历史得到清楚讲解时，游客会更加欣赏这座博物馆。","Speaking","Part 3 opinion"],["The report does not fully appreciate the financial burden on low-income families.","该报告没有充分认识低收入家庭承受的经济负担。","Writing","Task 2 critique"]]},
  { id:8,g:"g002",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"admit",linked:"recognize",ipa:"/ədˈmɪt/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to accept unwillingly that something is true, or allow someone to enter",coreZh:"承认（常含不情愿）；准许进入或接收入院",grammar:"admit that、admit doing/having done、admit someone to/into；不说 admit to do。",image:"一扇门先让人进入，随后一张嘴勉强说出事实。",c:[["admit that","承认……","The manufacturer admitted that the label was misleading.","制造商承认标签具有误导性。"],["be admitted to hospital","被收入院","Several residents were admitted to hospital after the fire.","火灾后数名居民被送入医院。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 admittere：ad-（向、进入）+ mittere（送），由“送入”发展出允许进入和承认。",family:["admission","admissible","admittedly"],bridge:"熟词桥：mission 含“送出”的 mit 意象；ad-mit 是送进门内。",scene:"门卫放人进门，证词也被法庭“放进记录”。",landing:"让人进入，或让一个不利事实进入公开记录。",brake:"承认做过某事用 admit doing；acknowledge 可中性承认，不一定不情愿。",micro:["Admit the visitor and admit the mistake.","准许访客进入，也承认错误。"],ie:[["Officials admitted that the new road had not reduced journey times.","官员承认新道路并未缩短出行时间。","Writing","Task 2 evidence"],["The patient was admitted to hospital for further observation.","患者被收入院接受进一步观察。","Listening","health context"]]},
  { id:9,g:"g002",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"identify",linked:"recognize",ipa:"/aɪˈdentɪfaɪ/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to establish exactly who or what something is, or select a cause, feature, or need",coreZh:"确认身份；查明并指出原因、特征或需求",grammar:"identify A as B、identify a cause/problem；identify with 表示认同，不等于识别。",image:"调查员给模糊对象贴上准确姓名和编号。",c:[["identify the cause","查明原因","Scientists are trying to identify the cause of the decline.","科学家正试图查明下降的原因。"],["identify A as B","确认A为B","The sample was identified as a previously unknown species.","该样本被确认是一种此前未知的物种。"]],origin:"来自 identity + -fy（使成为/认定为）；identity 最终关联拉丁语 idem（同一个）。",family:["identity","identification","identifiable"],bridge:"熟词桥：ID 是身份证明；identify 就是给对象确定 ID。",scene:"放大镜扫过脚印，屏幕弹出唯一编号。",landing:"从不确定对象中确定“究竟是哪一个”。",brake:"recognize 常凭旧记忆认出；identify 可以通过调查首次确定。",micro:["Identify it precisely, even if you have never seen it before.","即使以前没见过，也要准确确认它。"],ie:[["The study identified cost as the main barrier to higher education.","研究确认费用是接受高等教育的主要障碍。","Reading","finding"],["Candidates were asked to identify two features shown on the map.","考生被要求指出地图上的两个特征。","Listening","map task"]]},
  { id:10,g:"g002",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"comprehend",linked:"recognize",ipa:"/ˌkɒmprɪˈhend/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to understand a complex idea, situation, or consequence fully",coreZh:"充分理解复杂观点、情形或后果",grammar:"正式动词，接名词或 wh-/that 从句；通常不用进行时。",image:"两臂把散落的信息全部圈住，组成完整图景。",c:[["fully comprehend","充分理解","Few consumers fully comprehend the terms of the contract.","很少有消费者充分理解合同条款。"],["difficult to comprehend","难以理解","The scale of the ecological loss is difficult to comprehend.","生态损失的规模难以理解。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 comprehendere：com-（一起）+ prehendere（抓住），即“全部抓在一起”。",family:["comprehension","comprehensive","incomprehensible"],bridge:"熟词桥：comprehensive 是“全面的”；comprehend 是把信息全面抓住。",scene:"巨手把四散的拼图一把拢成完整地图。",landing:"不是仅知道，而是把复杂内容整体理解透。",brake:"recognize 可只是认出；comprehend 要达到较深、较完整的理解。",micro:["To comprehend the system is to grasp how its parts fit together.","理解这个系统，就是把握各部分如何衔接。"],ie:[["Readers must comprehend the writer's argument before evaluating the evidence.","读者必须先理解作者论点，才能评价证据。","Reading","argument"],["It is difficult to comprehend how quickly the coastline has changed.","海岸线变化之快令人难以理解。","Speaking","Part 3 response"]]},
  { id:11,g:"g003",type:"primary",word:"adjust",ipa:"/əˈdʒʌst/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to make a small change so that something works, fits, or responds better",coreZh:"微调，使更合适；适应",grammar:"adjust A、adjust A to B；人适应环境用 adjust to；adjust oneself to 较正式。",image:"手指旋动小旋钮，让模糊画面刚好清晰。",c:[["adjust the settings","调整设置","Users can adjust the settings to reduce energy use.","用户可以调整设置以降低能耗。"],["adjust to change","适应变化","New students often need time to adjust to independent study.","新生通常需要时间适应自主学习。"]],origin:"经古法语 ajuster，来自 a-（向）+ juste（正确、合适），即“使合适”。",family:["adjustment","adjustable","readjust"],bridge:"熟词桥：just 有“恰当”的旧义；adjust 是把东西调到恰当位置。",scene:"技师拧半圈旋钮，机器立刻平稳运行。",landing:"通常是为适配而做有限改变。",brake:"adjust 强调小幅适配；change 可大可小且不必为了适配。",micro:["Adjust the tool, then adjust to the new routine.","先调好工具，再适应新惯例。"],ie:[["Households adjusted their spending after energy prices rose.","能源价格上涨后，各家庭调整了支出。","Writing","Task 1 trend"],["It took me several weeks to adjust to the pace of university life.","我用了几周才适应大学生活的节奏。","Speaking","Part 1 experience"]]},
  { id:12,g:"g003",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"change",linked:"adjust",ipa:"/tʃeɪndʒ/",pos:"v.; n.",coreEn:"to become or make something different, sometimes substantially",coreZh:"改变；变化；更换",grammar:"change A、change from A to B、change into；作名词常用 a change in/to。",image:"旧路线被擦掉，整张地图重画。",c:[["change dramatically","发生巨大变化","Working patterns have changed dramatically since 2000.","自2000年以来，工作模式发生了巨大变化。"],["change from A to B","从A变为B","The land changed from farmland to residential use.","这片土地从农田变为住宅用地。"]],origin:"经古法语 changier 进入英语，更深来源通常联系晚期拉丁语 cambiare（交换）；细节仍有争议。",family:["changeable","unchanged","exchange"],bridge:"熟词桥：exchange 是互换；change 是状态或对象换掉。",scene:"舞台布景整套撤下，换成全新城市。",landing:"泛指变得不同，变化幅度不限。",brake:"只有小幅校准且目标是适配时，adjust 比 change 精确。",micro:["A change may replace the whole plan; an adjustment merely tunes it.","change 可换掉整个方案，adjust 往往只是微调。"],ie:[["The chart shows how household size changed over a twenty-year period.","图表显示二十年间家庭规模如何变化。","Writing","Task 1 overview"],["Climate change is altering both the timing and location of migration.","气候变化正在改变迁徙的时间和地点。","Reading","environment"]]},
  { id:13,g:"g003",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"modify",linked:"adjust",ipa:"/ˈmɒdɪfaɪ/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to alter part of something, usually to improve it or suit a new purpose",coreZh:"修改；改造（保留主体而改变部分）",grammar:"及物动词，常接 design, behaviour, diet, proposal；modify A to do/for B。",image:"保留房屋主体，只替换窗户和入口。",c:[["modify a design","修改设计","Engineers modified the design to improve ventilation.","工程师修改了设计以改善通风。"],["modify behaviour","改变行为","Small incentives may modify consumer behaviour.","小额激励可能改变消费者行为。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 modificare：modus（尺度、方式）+ facere（做），意为按尺度调整。",family:["modification","modified","modifiable"],bridge:"熟词桥：mode 是方式；modify 是改变做事方式或结构。",scene:"设计师不推倒房子，只移动门窗和墙。",landing:"局部变更，使原物适合新目标。",brake:"modify 通常保留主体；change 可能完全替换。",micro:["Modify the design without replacing the entire system.","修改设计，但不替换整个系统。"],ie:[["The questionnaire was modified after a small pilot study.","问卷在小规模试点研究后得到修改。","Reading","methodology"],["Cities could modify building codes to encourage natural ventilation.","城市可以修改建筑规范以鼓励自然通风。","Writing","Task 2 solution"]]},
  { id:14,g:"g003",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"shift",linked:"adjust",ipa:"/ʃɪft/",pos:"v.; n.",coreEn:"to move or cause attention, position, responsibility, or a pattern to move in a new direction",coreZh:"转移；移动；使重点或模式转向",grammar:"shift from A to B、shift attention/focus；作名词 a shift in/towards。",image:"聚光灯从舞台左侧缓慢移到右侧。",c:[["shift the focus","转移重点","The debate shifted the focus from cost to public safety.","这场辩论把重点从成本转向公共安全。"],["a shift towards","向……的转变","There has been a clear shift towards online banking.","人们已明显转向网上银行。"]],origin:"源自古英语 sciftan（安排、划分），属日耳曼语词源；不是透明的现代前后缀组合。",family:["shifting","shiftless","night shift"],bridge:"熟词桥：键盘 Shift 键让字符换挡；普通 shift 让位置或重点换挡。",scene:"巨型箭头把资源从城市中心推向郊区。",landing:"强调方向、位置或重心的转移。",brake:"shift 不是一般“改变”；它通常要能回答“从哪里转向哪里”。",micro:["The focus shifted from quantity to quality.","重点从数量转向了质量。"],ie:[["Employment shifted from manufacturing to service industries.","就业从制造业转向服务业。","Writing","Task 1 change"],["A slight shift in wind direction can affect air quality.","风向的轻微变化会影响空气质量。","Listening","weather context"]]},
  { id:15,g:"g003",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"alter",linked:"adjust",ipa:"/ˈɔːltə(r)/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to make something different, especially in character, condition, or appearance",coreZh:"改变性质、状态或外观",grammar:"及物或不及物；alter a plan/structure；conditions alter；较 change 正式。",image:"同一件外套被裁缝改短，整体仍是原件。",c:[["alter the balance","改变平衡","Tourism may alter the balance of the local economy.","旅游业可能改变当地经济的平衡。"],["substantially alter","大幅改变","The new evidence substantially altered the researchers' conclusion.","新证据大幅改变了研究人员的结论。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 alter（另一个、第二个），经法语进入英语；核心是使之成为“另一种状态”。",family:["alteration","alterable","unaltered"],bridge:"熟词桥：alternative 是“另一个选择”；alter 是把状态变成另一种。",scene:"一张政策海报被剪改后仍是原海报，却传达不同信息。",landing:"强调性质或状态发生改变，语体偏正式。",brake:"alter 不等于 alternate；alternate 是交替或轮流。",micro:["Alter the condition, not necessarily the whole object.","改变状态，不一定替换整个对象。"],ie:[["Road construction altered the natural flow of the river.","道路建设改变了河流的自然流向。","Reading","cause and effect"],["Working from home has altered how many people use city centres.","居家办公改变了许多人使用市中心的方式。","Writing","Task 2 analysis"]]},
  { id:16,g:"g004",type:"primary",word:"approach",ipa:"/əˈprəʊtʃ/",pos:"n.; v.",coreEn:"a way of dealing with a problem, or the act of moving nearer",coreZh:"处理问题的方法；接近",grammar:"方法义用 an approach to + n./doing；动词 approach 直接接宾语，不接 to。",image:"多条路线从不同方向通往同一座山。",c:[["an approach to learning","学习方法","The school adopted a flexible approach to language learning.","学校采用灵活的语言学习方法。"],["approach a problem","处理问题","Researchers approached the problem from several angles.","研究人员从多个角度处理这个问题。"]],origin:"经古法语 aprochier，来自晚期拉丁语 appropiare（靠近），与 prope（近）相关。",family:["approachable","approaching","reapproach"],bridge:"熟词桥：approach a station 是靠近车站；处理问题的 approach 是走近问题的路线。",scene:"三条小径以不同方式靠近山顶。",landing:"可指解决路线，也可指空间或时间上的接近。",brake:"名词后用 approach to；动词不说 approach to the building，而说 approach the building。",micro:["Choose an approach to the problem before you approach it.","在着手处理问题前，先选一种方法。"],ie:[["A community-based approach to recycling produced the best results.","以社区为基础的回收方法取得了最佳效果。","Reading","study finding"],["As the train approached the coast, the landscape became flatter.","火车接近海岸时，地势变得更平坦。","Listening","journey description"]]},
  { id:17,g:"g004",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"method",linked:"approach",ipa:"/ˈmeθəd/",pos:"n.",coreEn:"a systematic and often repeatable procedure for doing or studying something",coreZh:"系统、可复现的具体方法或步骤",grammar:"a method of/for doing；research method；method to do 可见但 of/for doing 更自然。",image:"实验台上按编号排列的一套操作步骤。",c:[["research method","研究方法","The paper explains its research method in detail.","论文详细说明了研究方法。"],["a method of measuring","测量方法","Scientists developed a reliable method of measuring soil moisture.","科学家开发了一种可靠的土壤湿度测量方法。"]],origin:"来自希腊语 methodos：meta-（追随）+ hodos（道路），即循路探究。",family:["methodology","methodical","methodically"],bridge:"熟词桥：methodology 是方法论；method 是其中一套具体程序。",scene:"研究员逐格勾选实验步骤，一次次得到相同结果。",landing:"强调明确步骤和可重复程序。",brake:"approach 可是总体理念；method 通常更具体、更程序化。",micro:["An approach gives direction; a method gives steps.","approach 给方向，method 给步骤。"],ie:[["The sampling method excluded households without internet access.","该抽样方法排除了无法上网的家庭。","Reading","method critique"],["One effective method of reducing waste is to charge for disposable bags.","减少浪费的一种有效方法是对一次性袋收费。","Writing","Task 2 solution"]]},
  { id:18,g:"g005",type:"primary",word:"fundamental",ipa:"/ˌfʌndəˈmentəl/",pos:"adj.; n.",coreEn:"forming the essential basis of something and necessary for it to exist or work",coreZh:"构成根基的；根本而必不可少的",grammar:"fundamental to；a fundamental principle/change；作复数 fundamentals 表示基本原理。",image:"整座建筑压在一块不可抽走的地基石上。",c:[["fundamental to","对……至关重要","Trust is fundamental to effective teamwork.","信任是有效团队合作的根本。"],["a fundamental change","根本性变化","The policy produced a fundamental change in land use.","该政策使土地利用发生根本性变化。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 fundamentum（基础），由 fundare（奠基）相关路径发展而来。",family:["fundamentally","fundamentals","foundation"],bridge:"熟词桥：foundation 是地基；fundamental 是位于概念地基上的。",scene:"抽掉一块写着“信任”的地基，整座合作大楼倒塌。",landing:"不是简单，而是不可缺少、支撑其余部分。",brake:"basic 可指初级；fundamental 强调构成根本，不一定简单。",micro:["A fundamental principle supports everything built above it.","根本原则支撑其上的一切。"],ie:[["Access to clean water is fundamental to public health.","获得清洁用水是公共健康的根本。","Writing","Task 2 claim"],["The discovery led to a fundamental change in our understanding of migration.","这一发现从根本上改变了我们对迁徙的理解。","Reading","scientific development"]]},
  { id:19,g:"g005",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"rudimentary",linked:"fundamental",ipa:"/ˌruːdɪˈmentri/",pos:"adj.",coreEn:"basic and not yet fully developed, often only enough for an elementary purpose",coreZh:"初步的；简陋而未充分发展的",grammar:"常修饰 knowledge, skill, system, equipment；通常含“发展不足”而非“最根本”。",image:"一架只有木框和两个轮子的原始机器。",c:[["rudimentary knowledge","粗浅知识","Many participants had only rudimentary knowledge of statistics.","许多参与者只有粗浅的统计知识。"],["a rudimentary system","简陋系统","The village had a rudimentary system for collecting rainwater.","村里有一套简陋的雨水收集系统。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 rudimentum（初步尝试、开端）；与 rudis（未加工、粗糙）相关。",family:["rudiment","rudiments","rudimentarily"],bridge:"熟词桥：the rudiments 是入门基础；rudimentary 是尚停留在入门阶段。",scene:"复杂机器的祖先只有木轮和绳子，却勉强能动。",landing:"基础且未成熟，常带“不完善”评价。",brake:"fundamental 是根本必需；rudimentary 是初级简陋，不能机械互换。",micro:["Rudimentary means basic because development has barely begun.","rudimentary 表示因发展刚起步而粗浅。"],ie:[["The settlement had only rudimentary sanitation facilities.","该聚居地只有简陋的卫生设施。","Reading","historical description"],["My first attempt relied on a rudimentary understanding of coding.","我的第一次尝试只依靠粗浅的编程知识。","Speaking","Part 2 reflection"]]},
  { id:20,g:"g005",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"preliminary",linked:"fundamental",ipa:"/prɪˈlɪmɪnəri/",pos:"adj.; n.",coreEn:"coming before the main stage in order to prepare, test, or provide an early indication",coreZh:"初步的；正式阶段之前的准备性工作",grammar:"preliminary findings/results/meeting；作名词常为 preliminaries（准备工作）。",image:"正式比赛前，计时器先跑一轮测试赛。",c:[["preliminary findings","初步发现","Preliminary findings suggest a link between noise and stress.","初步发现表明噪声与压力存在联系。"],["a preliminary survey","初步调查","A preliminary survey was conducted before the main study.","正式研究前进行了一项初步调查。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 prae-（在前）+ limen（门槛），意象是站在正式阶段门槛之前。",family:["preliminaries","preliminarily","liminal"],bridge:"熟词桥：pre- 表示“之前”；preliminary 是主阶段前的。",scene:"研究大门前摆着一张小型试验桌。",landing:"强调时间顺序上的前期和暂定。",brake:"preliminary 不是 fundamental：前者是“先做的”，后者是“支撑一切的”。",micro:["Preliminary results come first and may later change.","初步结果先出现，之后仍可能改变。"],ie:[["Preliminary data indicate that the intervention may reduce absenteeism.","初步数据显示该干预可能减少缺勤。","Writing","Task 1 report"],["After a preliminary interview, suitable volunteers joined the main trial.","初步面谈后，合适的志愿者加入了正式试验。","Listening","process"]]},
  { id:21,g:"g006",type:"primary",word:"rely on",ipa:"/rɪˈlaɪ ɒn/",pos:"phrasal v.",coreEn:"to need or trust someone or something for support, operation, or truth",coreZh:"依赖；信赖",grammar:"rely on/upon + 名词或动名词；rely on somebody to do；不可省略 on。",image:"一座桥把全部重量压在唯一桥墩上。",c:[["rely heavily on","严重依赖","Remote communities rely heavily on private cars.","偏远社区严重依赖私家车。"],["rely on evidence","依据证据","The conclusion relies on evidence from three long-term studies.","这一结论依据三项长期研究的证据。"]],origin:"rely 经古法语 relier，最终与拉丁语 religare（重新系紧）相关；现代搭配固定为 rely on。",family:["reliance","reliable","reliably"],bridge:"熟词桥：reliable 是“靠得住的”；rely on 就是把重量放到它上面。",scene:"整个村庄的电线都接到一块太阳能板上。",landing:"把支持、运行或判断建立在某来源上。",brake:"rely 后必须接 on/upon；不能说 rely something。",micro:["If a system relies on one source, that source must be reliable.","如果系统依赖单一来源，该来源就必须可靠。"],ie:[["Many rural households rely on wells for drinking water.","许多农村家庭依靠水井获取饮用水。","Reading","social infrastructure"],["I rely on public transport because parking near my office is expensive.","我依靠公共交通，因为办公室附近停车很贵。","Speaking","Part 1 routine"]]},
  { id:22,g:"g006",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"depend on",linked:"rely on",ipa:"/dɪˈpend ɒn/",pos:"phrasal v.",coreEn:"to be determined by, need support from, or vary according to something",coreZh:"取决于；依靠；视……而定",grammar:"depend on/upon + 名词/动名词；depend on whether/what；It depends. 可独立回答。",image:"天平读数随着下方条件卡片不断变化。",c:[["depend largely on","很大程度取决于","Success depends largely on consistent funding.","成功很大程度取决于持续资金。"],["depend on whether","取决于是否","The final route will depend on whether the bridge is open.","最终路线将取决于桥梁是否开放。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 dependere：de-（向下）+ pendere（悬挂），意象是“悬在某条件之上”。",family:["dependent","dependence","independent"],bridge:"熟词桥：pendant 是垂下的饰物；结果 depend on 条件，像悬挂在条件上。",scene:"一个结果牌被绳子吊在“资金”钩子上。",landing:"既可表示依赖，也常表示结果由条件决定。",brake:"rely on 更常强调信赖/依靠；depend on 更自然表达“取决于”。",micro:["The outcome depends on conditions; people may rely on support.","结果取决于条件，人则可能依靠支持。"],ie:[["The effectiveness of the policy depends on how strictly it is enforced.","政策效果取决于执行的严格程度。","Writing","Task 2 condition"],["Travel time depends on whether you take the coastal road.","出行时间取决于你是否走沿海公路。","Listening","route choice"]]},
  { id:23,g:"g007",type:"primary",word:"domestic",ipa:"/dəˈmestɪk/",pos:"adj.; n.",coreEn:"relating to the home or family, or occurring within one country rather than abroad",coreZh:"家庭的；国内的；驯养的",grammar:"domestic market/flights/violence/work；domestic animal；不能把 local 一律换成 domestic。",image:"一条国界把飞机、市场和家庭活动圈在内部。",c:[["domestic market","国内市场","The company sells most of its products in the domestic market.","该公司多数产品在国内市场销售。"],["domestic chores","家务","Technology has reduced the time spent on domestic chores.","技术减少了花在家务上的时间。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 domesticus，源自 domus（家）；由“家内”扩展到“国内”。",family:["domesticate","domestication","domestically"],bridge:"熟词桥：domesticated animals 是家养动物；domestic 的中心就是“家内/国境内”。",scene:"一座房子被放大成国家地图，所有活动都在屋内。",landing:"范围在家庭或本国之内。",brake:"local 是某地区当地；national 涉及整个国家；domestic 常与 international/foreign 对立。",micro:["Domestic can mean inside the home or inside the country.","domestic 可指家庭内部，也可指一国之内。"],ie:[["Domestic tourism increased when international travel was restricted.","国际旅行受限时，国内旅游增加了。","Writing","Task 1 trend"],["Shared appliances may reduce the time required for domestic work.","共享家电可能减少家务所需时间。","Reading","technology"]]},
  { id:24,g:"g008",type:"primary",word:"measure",ipa:"/ˈmeʒə(r)/",pos:"v.; n.",coreEn:"to determine size, amount, or degree using a standard; also an action taken for a purpose",coreZh:"测量；衡量；（名词）措施",grammar:"measure length/impact；measure A in B；作名词 take measures to do。",image:"尺子量长度，仪表盘同时衡量抽象影响。",c:[["measure the impact","衡量影响","The survey measured the impact of noise on sleep quality.","该调查衡量了噪声对睡眠质量的影响。"],["take measures to","采取措施","Authorities took measures to protect the wetland.","当局采取措施保护湿地。"]],origin:"经法语 mesure，来自拉丁语 mensura（测量），与 metiri（测量）相关。",family:["measurement","measurable","immeasurable"],bridge:"熟词桥：measurement 是测量结果；measure 是执行测量，也可指所采取的措施。",scene:"一把尺子从桌面伸到“教育效果”的仪表盘上。",landing:"用标准确定量或程度；名词也可指为目标采取的行动。",brake:"calculate 是算出数值；assess/evaluate 涉及判断；measure 未必做价值评价。",micro:["Measure the result, then decide what measures to take.","先测量结果，再决定采取什么措施。"],ie:[["Researchers measured air quality at twenty locations across the city.","研究人员在全市二十个地点测量了空气质量。","Reading","method"],["Governments should take measures to reduce single-use plastic.","政府应采取措施减少一次性塑料。","Writing","Task 2 solution"]]},
  { id:25,g:"g008",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"calculate",linked:"measure",ipa:"/ˈkælkjuleɪt/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to obtain a numerical result by using arithmetic or data",coreZh:"计算；根据数据推算",grammar:"calculate a cost/rate/distance；calculate that/how；常用 be calculated to。",image:"计算器把一串测量值变成最终数字。",c:[["calculate the cost","计算成本","Students calculated the total cost of the proposed scheme.","学生计算了拟议方案的总成本。"],["calculate a rate","计算比率","The rate was calculated using annual population data.","该比率用年度人口数据计算得出。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 calculare（用小石子计数），源自 calculus（小石子、计数石）。",family:["calculation","calculator","calculable"],bridge:"熟词桥：calculator 是计算器；calculate 是让它得出数字。",scene:"算盘上的小石子滚动，最后排成一个百分比。",landing:"通过算术或公式得出数值。",brake:"measure 先取得量；calculate 用测得的数据运算，二者步骤不同。",micro:["Measure the distance, then calculate the average speed.","先测距离，再计算平均速度。"],ie:[["The researchers calculated average household expenditure for each region.","研究人员计算了各地区的家庭平均支出。","Reading","data analysis"],["I calculated that commuting by train would save forty minutes a day.","我算出乘火车通勤每天能节省四十分钟。","Speaking","Part 3 explanation"]]},
  { id:26,g:"g008",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"assess",linked:"measure",ipa:"/əˈses/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to judge the condition, importance, ability, or risk of something using evidence",coreZh:"评估状况、重要性、能力或风险",grammar:"assess a risk/impact/need；assess whether/how；常含专业判断。",image:"评估员把证据放在量表上，给风险标级。",c:[["assess the risk","评估风险","Engineers assessed the risk of flooding before construction began.","工程师在施工前评估了洪水风险。"],["assess student performance","评估学生表现","The course uses projects to assess student performance.","该课程用项目评估学生表现。"]],origin:"经古法语 assesser，来自拉丁语 assidere（坐在旁边），历史上指评定税额；现代义已扩大。",family:["assessment","assessor","reassess"],bridge:"熟词桥：assessment 是评估；assess 是作出这种有依据的判断。",scene:"专家坐在证据旁，把风险从绿灯调到红灯。",landing:"根据标准和证据判断状态或风险。",brake:"measure 给出量；assess 把量与证据解释成判断。",micro:["Measure the level, then assess the risk it creates.","先测水平，再评估它造成的风险。"],ie:[["The team assessed whether the bridge could withstand stronger storms.","团队评估了该桥能否承受更强风暴。","Reading","engineering"],["Schools should assess creativity as well as factual knowledge.","学校应评估创造力，也应评估事实知识。","Writing","Task 2 opinion"]]},
  { id:27,g:"g008",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"evaluate",linked:"measure",ipa:"/ɪˈvæljueɪt/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to examine evidence and judge the quality, effectiveness, or value of something",coreZh:"评价质量、效果或价值",grammar:"evaluate a programme/effectiveness/evidence；常在收集数据后作综合价值判断。",image:"审查员把结果、成本和副作用放在同一架秤上。",c:[["evaluate effectiveness","评价有效性","The trial evaluated the effectiveness of online tutoring.","该试验评价了在线辅导的有效性。"],["critically evaluate","批判性评价","Students must critically evaluate the evidence presented.","学生必须批判性评价所呈现的证据。"]],origin:"由法语 évaluer 进入英语，核心来自 value（价值）；e-/ex- 历史成分表示引出价值判断。",family:["evaluation","evaluative","re-evaluate"],bridge:"熟词桥：value 是价值；evaluate 是判断价值或效果。",scene:"评审把数据、成本和质量打成一个综合分。",landing:"在分析证据后判断好坏、成效或价值。",brake:"assess 常判状态/风险；evaluate 更明确落到质量、效果或价值。",micro:["Evaluate the programme by judging what its measured results are worth.","通过判断测量结果的价值来评价项目。"],ie:[["The final report evaluated both the benefits and unintended effects of the policy.","最终报告评价了政策的益处和意外影响。","Reading","evaluation"],["Before expanding the scheme, the council should evaluate its cost-effectiveness.","扩大计划前，委员会应评价其成本效益。","Writing","Task 2 recommendation"]]},
  {id:28,g:"g009",type:"primary",word:"trait",ipa:"/treɪt/",pos:"n.",coreEn:"a particular quality in a person, organism, or group",coreZh:"（人、生物或群体的）特征、性状",grammar:"a trait of/in；personality/genetic trait；多指相对稳定特征。",image:"DNA链和人物档案上各亮起一个稳定标签。",c:[["personality trait","性格特征","Patience is a valuable personality trait in teachers.","耐心是教师宝贵的性格特征。"],["genetic trait","遗传性状","The study traced the genetic trait across generations.","研究追踪了这一遗传性状的代际传递。"]],origin:"经法语 trait（线条、特征），来自拉丁语 trahere（拉、画线）的历史路径。",family:["trait","portrait","traitor"],bridge:"熟词桥：portrait 用线条呈现面貌；trait 像人物或物种的一笔特征。",scene:"人物胸前挂着一枚写有“耐心”的永久徽章。",landing:"相对稳定且可辨认的个体或群体特征。",brake:"feature 可是物体任一突出部分；trait 常指人或生物稳定特性。",micro:["A trait is a relatively stable characteristic.","trait 是相对稳定的特征。"],ie:[["Curiosity is often regarded as an important trait in successful researchers.","好奇心常被视为成功研究者的重要特质。","Reading","claim"],["One trait I value in a colleague is reliability.","我重视同事身上的一个特质是可靠。","Speaking","Part 2 description"]]},
  {id:29,g:"g010",type:"primary",word:"coin",ipa:"/kɔɪn/",pos:"v.; n.",coreEn:"to invent a new word or phrase; also a piece of money",coreZh:"创造（新词或说法）；硬币",grammar:"coin a term/phrase/expression；常用被动 was coined by/in；不等于首次发现事物。",image:"铸币机把一个新词压印到金属片上。",c:[["coin a term","创造术语","A biologist coined the term to describe the new process.","一位生物学家创造了这个术语来描述新过程。"],["newly coined phrase","新造短语","The newly coined phrase spread rapidly online.","这个新造短语在网上迅速传播。"]],origin:"来自古法语 coin（楔形铸模），由“铸造硬币”比喻发展为创造词语。",family:["coinage","coiner","newly coined"],bridge:"熟词桥：硬币被模具铸出；新词也像被语言模具铸出。",scene:"印钞机吐出的不是钱，而是闪亮的新术语。",landing:"第一次创造并投入使用一个表达。",brake:"invent 可创造物件或方法；coin 通常限定新词语。",micro:["Writers coin terms as mints coin money.","作家创造术语，如同铸币厂铸造硬币。"],ie:[["The term was coined in the 1970s but became popular much later.","该术语创于20世纪70年代，但很久以后才流行。","Reading","history of an idea"],["I once coined a playful phrase that my friends still use.","我曾造过一个有趣短语，朋友们至今仍在用。","Speaking","Part 2 anecdote"]]},
  {id:30,g:"g011",type:"primary",word:"artificial",ipa:"/ˌɑːtɪˈfɪʃəl/",pos:"adj.",coreEn:"made by people rather than occurring naturally; sometimes not sincere",coreZh:"人造的；非天然的；不自然或虚假的",grammar:"artificial light/intelligence/materials；artificial smile；不必然表示劣质。",image:"塑料花在灯下看似真实，却没有根。",c:[["artificial light","人造光","Artificial light can disrupt sleep patterns.","人造光会扰乱睡眠模式。"],["artificial intelligence","人工智能","Artificial intelligence is changing medical diagnosis.","人工智能正在改变医学诊断。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 artificialis，源于 artificium：ars（技艺）+ facere（制作）。",family:["artifice","artificially","artificiality"],bridge:"熟词桥：art + facere 的意象是“用技艺做出来”。",scene:"一朵塑料花戴着“人造”标签却永不凋谢。",landing:"由人制作而非自然形成；语境决定褒贬。",brake:"synthetic 常强调化学合成；artificial 范围更广。",micro:["Artificial means made, not necessarily inferior.","artificial 表示人造，并不必然低劣。"],ie:[["Artificial lighting extended working hours but increased energy use.","人造照明延长了工作时间，却增加了能源使用。","Reading","technology"],["Some people worry that artificial intelligence will widen inequality.","有人担心人工智能会扩大不平等。","Writing","Task 2 discussion"]]},
  {id:31,g:"g012",type:"primary",word:"prompt",ipa:"/prɒmpt/",pos:"v.; adj.; n.",coreEn:"to cause or encourage a response; as an adjective, done without delay",coreZh:"促使、引发；及时的；提示",grammar:"prompt someone to do；prompt a reaction/debate；a prompt response；promptly 是副词。",image:"一个提示按钮被按下，立刻触发整排多米诺骨牌。",c:[["prompt a debate","引发辩论","The findings prompted a debate about data privacy.","这些发现引发了关于数据隐私的辩论。"],["prompt someone to do","促使某人做","Rising costs prompted families to save energy.","成本上涨促使家庭节能。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 promptus（准备好的、迅速的），是 promere（拿出、展示）的过去分词。",family:["promptly","promptness","prompter"],bridge:"熟词桥：电脑 prompt 是等待输入的提示；动词 prompt 会触发回应。",scene:"红色按钮一按，讨论和行动同时弹出。",landing:"外部刺激触发回应；形容词则强调不拖延。",brake:"initiate 是正式启动；prompt 强调某刺激促成反应；immediately 是副词而非同义词。",micro:["A prompt can prompt a prompt response.","一个提示可以促成及时回应。"],ie:[["The sharp increase in rent prompted many workers to move farther away.","租金猛涨促使许多工人搬到更远处。","Writing","Task 1 cause"],["A museum visit prompted me to learn more about local history.","一次博物馆参观促使我更多了解当地历史。","Speaking","Part 2 experience"]]},
  {id:32,g:"g013",type:"primary",word:"exchange",ipa:"/ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ/",pos:"v.; n.",coreEn:"to give one thing and receive another, or share information reciprocally",coreZh:"交换；互换；交流",grammar:"exchange A for B；exchange A with someone；an exchange of ideas；不等于单向 share。",image:"两只手同时跨过桌面互递不同物品。",c:[["exchange information","交换信息","Hospitals exchange information through a secure network.","医院通过安全网络交换信息。"],["exchange A for B","用A换B","Customers may exchange points for travel vouchers.","顾客可以用积分兑换旅行券。"]],origin:"ex-（出）+ change；change 经法语进入英语，历史核心与交换相关。",family:["exchangeable","interchange","exchanger"],bridge:"熟词桥：change 可表示零钱；exchange 是双方把东西换到对方手里。",scene:"两座岛同时把种子和工具抛给对方。",landing:"双向给予与获得。",brake:"share 可以共同使用且不要求回报；exchange 通常有双向性。",micro:["In an exchange, each side gives and receives.","exchange 中双方都有给予和获得。"],ie:[["The programme enables farmers to exchange information about crop diseases.","该项目使农民能够交流作物病害信息。","Reading","programme detail"],["Student exchanges can improve language skills and cultural awareness.","学生交流可提高语言能力和文化意识。","Writing","Task 2 example"]]},
  {id:33,g:"g013",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"apply A to B",linked:"exchange",ipa:"/əˈplaɪ eɪ tə biː/",pos:"verb pattern",coreEn:"to use a method, rule, substance, or idea on or in relation to a target",coreZh:"把A应用、施加到B上",grammar:"apply A to B；被动 A is applied to B；与 apply for a job、apply to a university 区分。",image:"把写有“方法A”的透明模板覆盖到问题B上。",c:[["apply a method to a problem","把方法用于问题","Researchers applied the method to a larger dataset.","研究人员把该方法用于更大的数据集。"],["apply pressure to","向……施加压力","The device applies gentle pressure to the injured area.","该设备向受伤部位施加轻微压力。"]],origin:"apply 来自拉丁语 applicare：ad-（向）+ plicare（折叠），历史意象是贴合。A/B 是教学槽位，不属于词形。",family:["application","applicable","applicant"],bridge:"熟词桥：application 是应用；apply A to B 就是把A贴合到B。",scene:"方法贴纸啪地贴到问题表面。",landing:"单向使用或施加，不是双方交换。",brake:"apply A to B 与 exchange 不同；原表候选关系属于题目替换线索而非真正同义。",micro:["Apply the method to the problem; do not exchange them.","把方法用于问题，不是交换二者。"],ie:[["The same model was applied to data from three countries.","同一模型被应用于三个国家的数据。","Reading","method"],["Schools could apply this approach to environmental education.","学校可把这种方法用于环境教育。","Writing","Task 2 proposal"]]},
  {id:34,g:"g014",type:"primary",word:"underlie",ipa:"/ˌʌndəˈlaɪ/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to form the hidden basis, cause, or principle of something",coreZh:"构成……的深层基础或原因",grammar:"及物动词：factors underlie a problem；过去式 underlay，过去分词 underlain。",image:"水面下的岩层支撑整座岛屿。",c:[["underlie a problem","构成问题根源","Several social factors underlie the housing crisis.","若干社会因素构成住房危机的根源。"],["principle underlying","背后的原则","The principle underlying the policy is fairness.","该政策背后的原则是公平。"]],origin:"透明复合词 under + lie；但不规则变化沿用 lie：underlay, underlain。",family:["underlying","underlay","underlain"],bridge:"熟词桥：lie under 是躺在下面；underlie 是在下面支撑。",scene:"一片看不见的根系托起地面上的森林。",landing:"隐藏在表象之下并形成基础。",brake:"underlie 是主动“构成基础”；be based on 是被动“建立在……之上”。",micro:["Hidden causes underlie visible problems.","隐藏原因构成可见问题的基础。"],ie:[["Economic insecurity underlies many of the reported health problems.","经济不安全是许多已报告健康问题的深层原因。","Reading","causal claim"],["Trust underlies any successful system of public cooperation.","信任是任何成功公共合作体系的基础。","Writing","Task 2 claim"]]},
  {id:35,g:"g014",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"based on",linked:"underlie",ipa:"/beɪst ɒn/",pos:"past-participle phrase",coreEn:"using something as the foundation, evidence, or source for a decision or statement",coreZh:"以……为基础或依据",grammar:"be based on evidence/data；based on 可作分词短语，但要避免悬垂修饰。",image:"一座结论塔稳稳立在证据地基上。",c:[["be based on evidence","以证据为依据","The recommendation is based on recent survey data.","该建议基于近期调查数据。"],["based on assumptions","基于假设","Forecasts based on weak assumptions may be misleading.","基于薄弱假设的预测可能误导。"]],origin:"base 经法语 base，来自希腊语 basis（脚步、基础）；on 标出承托关系。",family:["base","basis","basic"],bridge:"熟词桥：base 是底座；be based on 是把结论放在底座上。",scene:"证据砖块托着一座结论塔。",landing:"明示判断、设计或说法所依赖的依据。",brake:"underlie 的主语是基础因素；be based on 的主语是被支撑对象，句法方向相反。",micro:["Evidence underlies the conclusion; the conclusion is based on evidence.","证据支撑结论；结论以证据为基础。"],ie:[["The estimates are based on interviews with over two thousand households.","这些估算基于对两千多户家庭的访谈。","Reading","method"],["Policies should be based on reliable evidence rather than assumptions.","政策应以可靠证据而非假设为依据。","Writing","Task 2 principle"]]},
  {id:36,g:"g015",type:"primary",word:"ignore",ipa:"/ɪɡˈnɔː(r)/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to deliberately give no attention to someone, information, or a problem",coreZh:"故意不理会；忽视",grammar:"及物动词：ignore advice/a warning/someone；不接 to。",image:"警报灯闪烁，人物却转头戴上耳机。",c:[["ignore a warning","无视警告","Drivers who ignore flood warnings put others at risk.","无视洪水警告的司机会危及他人。"],["largely ignore","基本忽视","The report largely ignored the needs of older residents.","报告基本忽视了老年居民的需求。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 ignorare（不知道、不理会），与 ignarus（无知的）相关。",family:["ignorance","ignorant","ignorable"],bridge:"熟词桥：ignorant 是无知的；ignore 是把信息当作不知道。",scene:"红色警报在脸旁爆响，他却把它拖进垃圾桶。",landing:"通常含主动或有意不予关注。",brake:"overlook 常是无意漏看；neglect 常是未尽责任；underestimate 是低估而非不理。",micro:["Ignore means choose not to attend, not merely fail to notice.","ignore 是选择不理，不只是没注意到。"],ie:[["Policy makers cannot ignore the needs of an ageing population.","政策制定者不能忽视人口老龄化的需求。","Writing","Task 2 claim"],["The first survey ignored people without permanent addresses.","第一次调查忽略了没有固定地址的人。","Reading","method critique"]]},
  {id:37,g:"g015",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"neglect",linked:"ignore",ipa:"/nɪˈɡlekt/",pos:"v.; n.",coreEn:"to fail to give necessary care or attention, often over time",coreZh:"疏于照顾；玩忽；长期忽略应尽责任",grammar:"neglect duties/children/maintenance；neglect to do；也可作名词。",image:"一株本应浇水的植物长期枯萎。",c:[["neglect maintenance","疏于维护","The building deteriorated because owners neglected maintenance.","业主疏于维护，建筑因而恶化。"],["neglect to do","疏忽未做","The survey neglected to include part-time workers.","调查疏忽，未纳入兼职工人。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 neglegere：nec（不）+ legere（选择、收集），即没有选择去关注。",family:["neglectful","neglected","negligence"],bridge:"熟词桥：negligence 是疏忽；neglect 是长期未给予必要照料。",scene:"浇水壶就在旁边，植物却一周周枯萎。",landing:"该做的照料或责任没有做到。",brake:"ignore 可瞬间有意不理；neglect 常指持续失职或疏于照顾。",micro:["Neglect is failure to give the care that is due.","neglect 是未给予本应有的照料。"],ie:[["Years of neglect left the railway in poor condition.","多年的疏于维护使铁路状况很差。","Reading","infrastructure"],["Governments should not neglect preventive healthcare.","政府不应忽视预防性医疗。","Writing","Task 2 advice"]]},
  {id:38,g:"g015",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"overlook",linked:"ignore",ipa:"/ˌəʊvəˈlʊk/",pos:"v.",coreEn:"to fail to notice something; also to have a view over a place or forgive a fault",coreZh:"漏看；忽略；俯瞰；宽容过错",grammar:"overlook a detail/error；a room overlooks the sea；不要只记“忽视”。",image:"人从高处看遍城市，却漏掉脚边的小字。",c:[["overlook a detail","漏掉细节","The initial report overlooked a crucial difference between regions.","初步报告漏掉了地区间一个关键差异。"],["overlook the harbour","俯瞰港口","The apartment overlooks the harbour.","公寓俯瞰港口。"]],origin:"透明复合词 over + look；“从上看”发展出俯瞰，也发展出看过去而漏掉。",family:["overlooking","overlooked","lookout"],bridge:"熟词桥：look over 可检查；overlook 却可能目光越过去而漏掉。",scene:"望远镜看见远山，却跨过桌上关键数字。",landing:"常指无意漏看；另有俯瞰义。",brake:"ignore 常有意；overlook 多无意，而且可表示房间俯瞰景色。",micro:["You can overlook the sea and still overlook a detail.","你可以俯瞰大海，也可能漏掉一个细节。"],ie:[["The analysis overlooked seasonal differences in energy demand.","该分析忽略了能源需求的季节差异。","Reading","critique"],["Our hotel room overlooked a quiet public garden.","我们的酒店房间俯瞰一座安静的公共花园。","Speaking","Part 2 place"]]},
  {id:39,g:"g015",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"underestimate",linked:"ignore",ipa:"/ˌʌndərˈestɪmeɪt/",pos:"v.; n.",coreEn:"to judge an amount, difficulty, ability, or importance as lower than it really is",coreZh:"低估数量、难度、能力或重要性",grammar:"underestimate the cost/risk；do not underestimate；an underestimate of。",image:"小尺子量巨浪，只标出真实高度一半。",c:[["underestimate the cost","低估成本","Planners underestimated the cost of maintaining the tunnel.","规划者低估了隧道维护成本。"],["seriously underestimate","严重低估","The model seriously underestimated future demand.","该模型严重低估了未来需求。"]],origin:"under-（不足）+ estimate；estimate 来自拉丁语 aestimare（估价、判断）。",family:["underestimation","estimate","overestimate"],bridge:"熟词桥：estimate 是估算；under- 让估算落在真实值之下。",scene:"估算尺只量到巨浪腰部。",landing:"注意到了对象，却给出的判断过低。",brake:"underestimate 不是 ignore：前者做了判断但偏低，后者干脆不理会。",micro:["To underestimate is to estimate too low, not to ignore.","underestimate 是估得过低，不是完全忽视。"],ie:[["Early forecasts underestimated the speed of urban growth.","早期预测低估了城市增长速度。","Reading","data comparison"],["People often underestimate how much sleep teenagers need.","人们常低估青少年需要的睡眠量。","Speaking","Part 3 opinion"]]},
  {id:40,g:"g016",type:"primary",word:"fertiliser",ipa:"/ˈfɜːtəlaɪzə(r)/",pos:"n.",coreEn:"a natural or manufactured substance added to soil to help plants grow",coreZh:"肥料（可天然，也可人工制造）",grammar:"British spelling fertiliser；US fertilizer；chemical/organic fertiliser；不可默认等于 toxic chemical。",image:"土壤得到养分颗粒后长出茂盛作物。",c:[["chemical fertiliser","化肥","Excessive chemical fertiliser can pollute rivers.","过量化肥会污染河流。"],["organic fertiliser","有机肥","The farm uses compost as an organic fertiliser.","该农场把堆肥用作有机肥。"]],origin:"fertile + -ise + -er；fertile 来自拉丁语 fertilis（多产的），与 ferre（承载、产生）相关。",family:["fertile","fertilise","fertility"],bridge:"熟词桥：fertile soil 是肥沃土壤；fertiliser 让土壤更肥沃。",scene:"养分袋给贫瘠土壤充电，庄稼立即长高。",landing:"为植物提供养分的物质，不限定天然或化学。",brake:"fertiliser 不等于 toxic；毒性取决于成分、剂量与使用方式。",micro:["Fertiliser feeds plants; misuse may still harm ecosystems.","肥料给植物提供养分，但误用仍可能伤害生态。"],ie:[["Farmers reduced fertiliser use without lowering crop yields.","农民减少了肥料使用，却没有降低产量。","Reading","agriculture"],["Subsidies could encourage the careful use of organic fertiliser.","补贴可鼓励谨慎使用有机肥。","Writing","Task 2 policy"]]},
  {id:41,g:"g016",type:"highlighted_substitute",word:"toxic",linked:"fertiliser",ipa:"/ˈtɒksɪk/",pos:"adj.",coreEn:"poisonous or capable of causing serious harm; figuratively, extremely harmful",coreZh:"有毒的；造成严重伤害的",grammar:"toxic to humans/wildlife；toxic chemicals/waste；比喻 toxic relationship/culture。",image:"红色骷髅标志从液体容器上冒出。",c:[["toxic to wildlife","对野生动物有毒","The substance is highly toxic to aquatic wildlife.","该物质对水生野生动物有剧毒。"],["toxic waste","有毒废物","The factory was fined for dumping toxic waste.","工厂因倾倒有毒废物被罚。"]],origin:"来自拉丁语 toxicum（毒药），更早源于希腊语 toxikon（箭毒），与 toxon（弓）相关。",family:["toxicity","toxin","nontoxic"],bridge:"熟词桥：toxin 是毒素；toxic 是会造成毒害的。",scene:"一支古箭蘸着毒液，旁边亮起骷髅警告。",landing:"物质或环境具有毒害性；不是“人造”的同义词。",brake:"chemical、unnatural、fertiliser 都不自动等于 toxic；必须有毒害证据。",micro:["A chemical fertiliser may be harmful, but it is not automatically toxic.","化肥可能有害，但并不自动等于有毒。"],ie:[["Toxic pollutants accumulated in fish near the industrial zone.","有毒污染物在工业区附近的鱼体内积累。","Reading","environment"],["Stricter rules are needed for the disposal of toxic waste.","有毒废物处置需要更严格的规定。","Writing","Task 2 solution"]]},
  {id:42,g:"g017",type:"primary",word:"that*",ipa:"/ðæt; ðət/",pos:"pron.; determiner; conj.; relative marker",coreEn:"a form used to point to, refer back to, introduce content, or link a defining relative clause",coreZh:"指示“那个”；回指前文；引导从句或限定性定语从句",grammar:"星号是源表考点标记，不属于拼写。that 可作指示词、代词、连接词或关系词；先判断所指对象。",image:"一根箭头跨过句子，精准指回前文信息。",c:[["evidence that","……的证据/这一事实","There is evidence that green space improves wellbeing.","有证据表明绿地改善幸福感。"],["the method that","……的方法（限定）","The method that produced the best result was inexpensive.","产生最佳结果的方法成本不高。"]],origin:"that 源自古英语 þæt，属日耳曼语指示词系统；星号仅为教材标记。",family:["that","this","those","these"],bridge:"熟词桥：this/these 指较近；that/those 常指较远或已提及信息。",scene:"句子里的 that 发射激光，指回唯一名词。",landing:"核心任务是建立指代或从句连接。",brake:"阅读时不要机械翻成“那个”；先判定其词性和指代范围。",micro:["Ask what that points to before translating it.","翻译 that 前先问它指向什么。"],ie:[["The survey found that commuters valued reliability above speed.","调查发现通勤者重视可靠性胜过速度。","Reading","reference tracking"],["The library that opened last year is already overcrowded.","去年开放的图书馆已经过于拥挤。","Writing","relative clause"]]},
  {id:43,g:"g018",type:"primary",word:"and*",ipa:"/ænd; ənd/",pos:"conj.",coreEn:"a coordinator linking equivalent words, phrases, clauses, or related additions",coreZh:"连接并列成分；表示递进、顺承或相关补充",grammar:"星号为教材标记。and 两侧应保持语法平行；注意 both…and、not only…but also 等成对结构。",image:"一座桥把两个同等高度、同样形状的结构连起来。",c:[["both A and B","A和B两者","Both cost and reliability influence travel choices.","成本和可靠性都会影响出行选择。"],["not only A but also B","不仅A而且B","The scheme not only saved money but also reduced waste.","该计划不仅省钱，还减少了浪费。"]],origin:"源自古英语 and，属日耳曼语基本连词；星号不是词的一部分。",family:["and","both…and","not only…but also"],bridge:"熟词桥：and 像等号桥，桥两侧结构要平行。",scene:"两节同型号车厢由 and 挂钩连接。",landing:"把语法地位相同或逻辑相关的内容并列。",brake:"and 不表示选择或对立；检查两侧词性和结构是否平行。",micro:["And links equals: noun and noun, clause and clause.","and 连接同级：名词与名词，从句与从句。"],ie:[["The policy reduced congestion and improved air quality.","该政策缓解了拥堵并改善了空气质量。","Writing","compound predicate"],["Participants were asked to record both distance and travel time.","参与者被要求同时记录距离和出行时间。","Listening","instruction"]]},
  {id:44,g:"g019",type:"primary",word:"rather than*",ipa:"/ˈrɑːðə ðæn/",pos:"contrastive phrase",coreEn:"used to prefer or identify one alternative instead of another",coreZh:"而不是；取A舍B",grammar:"星号为教材标记。保持平行：noun rather than noun / do rather than do；注意 would rather A than B。",image:"岔路口的箭头明确选择A并划掉B。",c:[["A rather than B","A而非B","The decline reflected lower demand rather than limited supply.","这一下降反映的是需求降低，而非供应受限。"],["do A rather than do B","做A而不是做B","Many residents cycle rather than drive short distances.","许多居民短途出行骑车而不开车。"]],origin:"rather 源自古英语 hraþor（更快、更宁愿），than 源自比较连词；星号非词形。",family:["rather","rather than","would rather…than"],bridge:"熟词桥：would rather 是宁愿；rather than 把偏好放在A而不是B。",scene:"天平把A保留在台上，把B弹进回收箱。",landing:"明确否定替代项B并选择或解释A。",brake:"rather than 不是普通转折 but/however；它表达替代或纠正。",micro:["Choose A rather than B, and keep A and B parallel.","选择A而非B，并保持A、B结构平行。"],ie:[["The improvement resulted from better maintenance rather than new construction.","改善源于更好的维护，而不是新建工程。","Reading","cause distinction"],["Cities should improve existing parks rather than remove them.","城市应改善现有公园，而不是拆除它们。","Writing","Task 2 recommendation"]]},
];

